face-image: img/sklarek.jpg

= The Housing Contracts Affair

Prosecutors have raided the offices of a construction company that built thousands of social housing flats for one of our Länder governments. Investigators say that it paid for holidays, consultancy contracts and party sponsorship in return for contracts at inflated prices. Two of the officials involved are SPD members, and a state secretary has close ties to the company. The AfD calls it proof that "the old parties" are all corrupt.

The Landtag has set up a committee of inquiry. What should be our posture?

- @downplay
- @corruption_unacceptable
- @turn_back

@corruption_unacceptable
title: Corruption is unacceptable. Cooperate fully with the investigation, even if it implicates the SPD.
on-arrival: center_dissent += 5; reformist_dissent += 5; labor_dissent += 5; trust_in_democracy += 1

We cooperate fully, the state secretary resigns, and members credibly accused of corruption are suspended from the party. Some loyal comrades feel betrayed, but the damage to the party is limited.

@downplay
title: Downplay the affair.
on-arrival: workers_spd -= 1; new_middle_spd -= 2; old_middle_spd -= 2; rural_spd -= 2; catholics_spd -= 2; unemployed_spd -= 2; trust_in_democracy -= 2; afd_relation -= 2

We speak of a few individual failings and act only when we are forced to. Every new revelation in the press damages us further, and people are increasingly disillusioned with politics.

@turn_back
title: The company also sponsored other parties. Make that known.
choose-if: judicial_reform > 1 and federal_police_loyalty > 0.5
unavailable-subtitle: We cannot prove it without stronger prosecutors and police.
on-arrival: new_middle_spd -= 1; old_middle_spd -= 1; rural_spd -= 1; catholics_spd -= 1; new_middle_cdu -= 1; old_middle_cdu -= 1; new_middle_fdp -= 1; trust_in_democracy -= 2

The investigation shows that the company sponsored the Union and the FDP just as generously. The scandal now touches every established party.

Only the AfD and the BSW appear untouched.
